---
layout: null
permalink: /assets/data/pnec-nav.json
sitemap: false
---
{%- comment -%}
  Jekyll-emitted JSON of the data-driven nav. This is what assets/js/
  pnec-nav-patch.js fetches at runtime to rewrite the WP-cloned nav on
  the marketing pages (about.html, programs-and-services.html, etc.)
  which can't pick up the include-level refactor because they don't
  use a Jekyll layout. After a save in /pages/admin-nav.html, GitHub
  Pages rebuilds and this file refreshes — and the marketing-page nav
  updates within ~2 min of save.
{%- endcomment -%}
{
  "items": [
    {%- assign nav_items = site.data.pnec_nav -%}
    {%- for item in nav_items -%}
    {
      "title": {{ item.title | jsonify }},
      "url": {{ item.url | jsonify }},
      "match": {{ item.match | default: "" | jsonify }},
      "external": {{ item.external | default: false | jsonify }}
    }{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  ]
}
